   "createdAt": "2026-07-26T00:32:05.040183+00:00",
   "content": "**Putting is the clearest team-wide leak to address this week.**\n\nAll 7 players are giving back strokes on the greens, and the deficit is larger than any other measured area:\n\n| Player | SG Putting (rounds) | SG Approach (rounds) | 3-putt rate |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Cole Bennett | -3.91 (15) | -1.54 (15) | 10.34% |\n| Jackson Hale | -3.91 (15) | -1.54 (15) | 10.34% |\n| Tyler Hayes | -3.34 (11) | -2.68 (11) | 10.61% |\n| Mason Rivers | -3.00 (12) | -2.44 (12) | 8.80% |\n| Dylan Brooks | -3.00 (12) | -2.03 (12) | 8.80% |\n| Ethan Park | -2.72 (13) | -2.97 (13) | 9.78% |\n| Owen Carter | -2.16 (12) | -3.83 (12) | 7.87% |\n\nWindows run roughly late May through mid-July for each player, per-player sample sizes as shown. Team average SG putting is about -3.15/round versus -2.43/round for approach, so putting is the bigger group-wide gap right now.\n\nThis lines up with what's already flagged individually: Cole Bennett, Jackson Hale, and Dylan Brooks each have an open \"lag putts → 3-putt cascade\" focus area, and Cole and Owen both have specific make-rate targets inside 10 feet. Owen Carter is the one exception where approach (-3.83) outweighs putting (-2.16) as his bigger leak — worth a word to him individually rather than folding him into a group putting block.\n\nGiven the Spring Preview Tournament starts Wednesday (July 30, Magnolia Ridge), a lag-putting and 3-putt-avoidance session this week is well timed — it's the fastest lever before you tee it up, and it's showing up for the whole roster, not just one or two guys.\n\nSeparately: Dylan Brooks and Jackson Hale haven't RSVP'd for that tournament yet, and there are two overdue tasks (yardage book update, swing assessment video) that predate the trip — worth a nudge if you haven't already.\n\nWant me to draft a recurring practice block for this week built around lag putting / 3-putt drills?\n\n_Some figures in this answer could not be traced back to your program's data, so I've flagged it rather than presenting them as fact. Please ask again._",
